.TITLE "top"

.DIV "DESCRIPTION"
Displays real-time system statistics. It provides a dynamic view of __process activity__, CPU usage, memory consumption, and system load.

.DIV "ALIAS"

.DIV "TLDR"
**top**
Displays a live list of system processes and resource usage.
> 

**top -o cpu**
Sorts the process list by CPU usage in descending order.
> __-o__ order flag | __cpu__ sort criteria

**top -o mem**
Sorts the process list by memory usage.
> __-o__ order flag | __mem__ sort criteria

**top -u**
Sorts the display by the actual CPU time used by each process.
> __-u__ CPU time flag

**top -s 5**
Updates the display every five seconds instead of the default interval.
> __-s__ samples flag | __5__ seconds

.DIV "SUMMARY"
The macOS version of __top__ is unique and uses different flags than the Linux version. While __top__ is useful for a quick glance, many macOS users prefer the __Activity Monitor__ application for a more detailed graphical interface.

.DIV "SEE ALSO"
**mac:ps** **mac:kill**

